<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The People United Will Never Be Defeated! (Frederic Rzewski)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1975</span><span class="sg-chain-h">36 piano variations</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Barpakhiz (Iranian revolutionaries)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1979</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, Persian words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">El pueblo unido (Hannes Wader)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1977</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover, German live album</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Horo da opozicio (Gianfranco Molle, translation by Renato Corsetti)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1978</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Esperanto translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Awit ng Tagumpay (Patatag)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">loose Tagalog translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ballad of the Fallen (Charlie Haden, Carla Bley, Liberation Music Orchestra)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1982</span><span class="sg-chain-h">jazz version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Resistance March, Argentina</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1983</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new words for the disappeared</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Fırtınadan Önce (Mehmet Celal)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1999</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Turkish version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Razom nas bahato (GreenJolly)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2004</span><span class="sg-chain-h">paraphrase; Ukraine's Eurovision entry, 2005</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Chinese translation (Huáng Sī-nóng and Jiăng Tāo)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2014</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation, Sunflower Student Movement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Control (Big Sean with Kendrick Lamar and Jay Electronica)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2013</span><span class="sg-chain-h">samples the Ortega and Quilapayún recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Geniş Merdiven</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2022</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted Turkish translation</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Speech of Jorge Eliécer Gaitán</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1940s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of the title phrase</span></li></ul></section>
